This port directly compiles the original common/party/server-core/applicable version
Java sources, resources and libraries. Bedrock lifecycle, platform adapters,
transparent-window composition and perspective lyric-stage host are added.
Minecraft-only loader/mixins/protocol paths are excluded. Platform overlays are
generated by tools/prepare_jvm_sources.py. Public font resource replacements are
explicitly recorded in the upstream source manifest; applicable Java source
remains pinned and unchanged before platform overlays.
WorldLyricsState/WorldLyricsRenderer/glyph effects and NCMScreen remain upstream.
The view-following stage remains selectable. A read-only exact-version native
camera adapter adds world-positioned lyrics to the owned layer; neither mode
creates a Minecraft world object or uses the game depth buffer. Optional partial voxel occlusion is a Bedrock host adaptation, not native depth.
Legacy native UI/network code remains in source for reference, not the active UI.

Third-party Java/native dependencies are distributed in jvm/lib. Their licenses
and original embedded notices are in licenses/dependencies. Additional full
texts include Skia BSD, Processing Sound LGPL 2.1, and Mozilla MPL 2.0.
Repackaged Processing Sound remains LGPL-covered. It is not relicensed under
Apache. Corresponding reusable upstream source and Bedrock modifications/build
files are supplied in the versioned sources/MuoniumPlayerBedrock-*-sources.zip.
Replace/relink the Java components under their respective license terms.
No restriction is intended on modifications or reverse engineering needed for
debugging those modifications. Details/source links: docs/DEPENDENCIES.md.

Public text fonts are unmodified Noto Sans and Noto Sans CJK, SIL OFL 1.1.
They replace SF Pro/PingFang while retaining historical resource aliases.
Full OFL notices and pinned provenance are in the host JAR and source resources
under META-INF/licenses/public-fonts/. Original icon fonts/artwork retain their
upstream attribution. Platform marks identify supported services only.
Third-party assets and optional backends retain their respective terms.

The bundled minimal Java runtime derives from Oracle JDK 21.0.5. Keep its
runtime/legal and runtime/release files; those distribution terms still apply.
The runtime can be replaced with a compatible licensed JDK 21 jlink runtime.

